kie","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10874","person_slug":"rebekha-sharkie","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rob Mitchell","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10733","person_slug":"rob-mitchell","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sally Sitou","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10995","person_slug":"sally-sitou","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sam Lim","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11000","person_slug":"sam-lim","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sam Rae","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10982","person_slug":"sam-rae","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sharon Claydon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10805","person_slug":"sharon-claydon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Shayne Neumann","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10485","person_slug":"shayne-neumann","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Bates","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10970","person_slug":"stephen-bates","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Georganas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10245","person_slug":"steve-georganas","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Susan Templeman","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10873","person_slug":"susan-templeman","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tania Lawrence","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10981","person_slug":"tania-lawrence","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Watts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10794","person_slug":"tim-watts","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Burke","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10081","person_slug":"tony-burke","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tracey Roberts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10994","person_slug":"tracey-roberts","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zali Steggall","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10941","person_slug":"zali-steggall","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zaneta Mascarenhas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10999","person_slug":"zaneta-mascarenhas","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zoe Daniel","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10979","person_slug":"zoe-daniel","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Governor-General Amendment (Salary) Bill 2024 - Second Reading - Agree with the bill's main idea","noes":7,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debates/?id=2024-06-25.95.2) to agree with the main idea of the bill. In parliamentary jargon, they voted to read the bill for a second time. ### What does this bill do? According to the [explanatory memorandum](https://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fems%2Fr7184_ems_9ad3b3b2-0ea3-4968-a2e0-5bf75ee1ed41%22) (which is a document prepared by the government): > *The [Governor-General Amendment (Salary) Bill 2024](https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r7184) amends the Governor-General Act 1974 to set the salary for the next Governor-General, Ms Samantha Mostyn AC, prior to her swearing-in on 1 July 2024.* > > *Section 3 of the Constitution provides that the salary of the Governor-General shall not be altered during their continuance in office. The Bill amends the Governor-General Act to change the sum payable for the salary of the Governor-General from $495,000 to $709,017.* > > *In line with past practice, the proposed salary is calculated by reference to the estimated average salary of the Chief Justice of the High Court of Australia over the notional five-year term of the appointment of the Governor-General. Where, in the past, a Governor-General has been the recipient of other Commonwealth entitlements - such as a judicial pension - the annual salary has been adjusted accordingly. Ms Mostyn is not a recipient of any such entitlements.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-8963","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2024-06-25/1"}
